      "hasMediaInOriginal": true,
      "fallbackReason": null,
      "text": "Google is working on an 'Enhanced HDR brightness' setting that lets you control how much HDR content brightens your Pixel's screen\n\nThis new setting will be found under Settings &gt; Display & touch &gt; Enhanced HDR brightness and includes a toggle to disable HDR support entirely as well as a slider to adjust the HDR effect's intensity. The page includes a standard image and a HDR image to compare the before/after.  \n\nThis setting isn't available in Android 16 QPR1 Beta 1 but will likely be available later.\n\n🔗 https://www.androidauthority.com/android-16-qpr1-enhanced-hdr-brightness-setting-3563653/",
      "links": [
        {
          "label": "https://www.androidauthority.com/android-16-qpr1-enhanced-hdr-brightness-setting-3563653/",
          "url": "https://www.androidauthority.com/android-16-qpr1-enhanced-hdr-brightness-setting-3563653/"
        }
