          "url": "https://cdn4.telesco.pe/file/TloP6FBfjATdL1qnbUJBYLXYWGifMlNjP6YJY8aE0RSKZuxMKX726JKw2GQeETMAdqrdHXYpHE2VQPl2yXibFnjzoRa3kLXwTuQ-51UZf0hFmWHI-8V7Lkaw8sdX6Ub1d_19Mt1H58fVJgzoiKCM86hPxj3JYo48Ji6nz80yYLXO-csFzoeZME9ZAwWCQITe-hN5n7OxjOyU3ooPZayNzZ50srxJ_qUlBQQriq3dSnzJckdnrz40dE8g0NV04r3WL0Qit8T1yFE2oDw3zGIsp64EEySVOvlNoLpux3qeW61Ea__-8wgEjo0DSxHYR8AuKAYHDNSlVV4OQeW_HBtHnw.jpg"
        }
      ],
      "hasMediaInOriginal": true,
      "fallbackReason": null,
      "text": "Pixel devices will finally get native flashlight strength adjustment. \n\nWhile Android has had an API for flashlight brightness control since Android13, Google only used it in the Camera and Magnifier apps. Until now, Pixel owners had to rely on third-party apps that utilizes this API to adjust Pixel's flashlight intensity.\n\nBut that could change soon, as Google is working on integrating a \"Flashlight Strength\" slider directly into the quick settings tile. When active, the tile will even show the current brightness percentage.\n\nThe brightness adjustment menu is invoked by either tapping the right side of the tile (for the wide variant) or holding the tile (for the shortened tile variant),  which immediately turns on the flashlight.\n\nWe'll probably see this change in Android 16 QPR1. \n\n😎 Google News | En",
      "links": [
        {
          "label": "since Android13",
          "url": "https://t.me/google_nws/1693"
        },
