      },
      "text": "📷 Pixel 9 series has gained the ability to connect external cameras. \n\nThe new Connected Cameras feature allows for seamless capture or live streaming using remote cameras. A camera selection tool will appear on the screen to switch between them. \n\n• Devices you can connect as a remote camera: Pixel 6 and newer, GoPro 10 and newer (with updated software)\n• Supported apps: Facebook, YouTube, Instagram, Snapchat, TikTok\n\nYou can activate the feature under Settings / Connected Devices / Connected preferences / Connected cameras. The latest versions of the Pixel Camera Services app (v.2.2) and Cross device Services are required. \n\nImportant Clarifications:\n• Available only for Pixel 9, Pixel 9 Pro, Pixel 9 Pro XL, and Pixel 9 Pro Fold.\n• You can only connect to devices that are authorized with your Google Account.\n• You can only connect to one remote camera at a time, to connect another remote camera, you’ll need to disconnect the first remote camera.\n• Audio is sourced from the camera that is currently in use.\n• Using a Bluetooth audio source may degrade the streaming quality.\n\nThe feature may take a few weeks to become available. \n\n🔗 Support Page \n\n😎 Google News | En",
